# Enginuity Coding Context

- Treat Supabase SQL migrations in `supabase/migrations/` as the database schema source of truth.
- Regenerate `src/sharedModules/services/supabase/database.types.ts` after schema changes using `yarn db:types`.
- Keep DB structure changes in migrations; keep seed/demo data in `supabase/seed.sql`.
- Prefer typed `SupabaseClient<Database>` usage; avoid `any` and temporary casts unless blocked.
- Before coding, align with existing modules/services conventions instead of introducing parallel patterns.

# Delivery Defaults

- Make focused, reviewable changes with clear rationale.
- Add or update tests when behavior changes and tests provide regression value.
- Keep naming and folder conventions consistent with existing repo structure.
